Purchases

How do I remove ads?
Open the Store from the main menu or the pause menu. "Remove Ads" is the first card at the top, priced at $1.99. It is a one-time purchase that turns off the bottom banner and the full screen interstitial ads. Optional rewarded videos stay available, because those are ones you choose to watch for a reward.

How do I restore my purchases?
Open the Store, then tap "Restore Purchases" at the bottom. Restoring uses the Apple ID that made the original purchase and brings back Remove Ads and the Starter Pack. Drops you bought are consumable, so they are delivered once and are not restorable; your current balance is kept on your device.

I bought something and did not receive it.
Tap "Restore Purchases" in the Store first. If it still does not appear, email us with the date of purchase and the Apple receipt, and we will sort it out.

Ads

Why do I see a banner at the bottom?
Ads keep the game free. The banner sits below the play area and never covers the lives counter or the level timer. Buying Remove Ads hides it permanently.

When do full screen ads appear?
Only after positive moments: finishing a level, or closing an unlock celebration. They never appear when you lose a life, fall, run out of lives, or retry. There is also a long cooldown between them.

What are the "watch an ad" offers?
They are optional. You can watch a short video to keep going after running out of lives, to restart from the last checkpoint, to refill your power-ups and lives from the pause menu, to claim a free power-up pack, or to try a locked ball skin for one level. Nothing is taken from you if you decline.

Privacy and tracking

How do I change my tracking choice?
Open Settings inside the game and look under "Privacy & Ads". If you have not answered the tracking prompt yet, the "Privacy & Tracking" row shows it again. Once you have answered it, iOS does not allow an app to reset that prompt, so the row opens the iOS Settings page for Precision Drop instead, where you can change it under Privacy & Security, Tracking.

How do I change my ad consent choices?
Where your region requires a consent message, a "Privacy Options" row appears in the same Settings section. Tap it to reopen the choices.

Progress

My progress was lost.
Progress is saved on your device only. Deleting and reinstalling the App clears it, and it cannot be recovered. Your Game Center leaderboard times are tied to your Apple ID and survive a reinstall.

The game crashes or will not load.
Close the App completely and reopen it. Make sure you are on the latest version from the App Store, and try restarting your device. If it persists, email us with your device model and iOS version.

